# Deploy to meshmap test host after changes

When you change Nodographer **frontend** files (HTML/CSS/JS/images under `frontend/`), **always copy them to the meshmap test web host in the same turn** so they can be tested immediately. Do not wait to be asked.

## Host (test deploy target)

- URL: http://k1rks-testmap.local.mesh/meshmap/ (canonical test meshmap)
- SSH: `k1rks-testmap` (user `meshmap`)
- Docroot: `/srv/meshmap/frontend/` (also linked from `/var/www/html/meshmap`)
- Full `/srv/meshmap` install on this host (frontend; meshinfo data may be proxied)

## How

- `scp` changed files into `/tmp/` then `cp` into the matching paths under `/srv/meshmap/frontend/` (`js/`, `css/`, `images/`, `index.html`, etc.)
- `chmod 644` on installed files (owner is typically `meshmap`)
- Verify with `grep` or file presence, then tell the user to hard-refresh at the URL above

## Do not

- Deploy secrets, `.ssh*`, `.deploy-stage/`, or `reports/`
- Use `public-meshmap-meshweb` as the default test target (use `k1rks-testmap` / the URL above)
- Skip host deploy just because git commit/push was not requested; still deploy for testing
